    ],
    "lyrics": {
      "text": "By the in-ter-ces-sions of Thy Mar-tyrs, O Lord, grant rest un-to the souls of Thy ser-vants.\n\nO_ life-be-stow-ing Lord of all, law-ful-ly did Thy Mar-tyrs strive in con-test, and now, a-dorned by Thee with vic-tors’ crowns, they ask e-ter-nal re-demp-tion for all the faith-ful that have left this__ life.__\n\nTheir souls shall dwell a-mong good__ things.\n\nThou didst in-struct me gone a-stray by man-y signs and won-ders, which Thou wrought-est a-fore-time; but now at the end of time, Thou both didst emp-ty Thy-self and, as mer-ci-ful, didst seek and find and__ save.__\n\nGlo-ry to the Fa-ther, and to the Son, and to the Ho--ly Spir-it.\n\nO_ Good One, grant all who have passed o-ver to Thee from out of the un-sta-ble and swift-ly-mov-ing course of fleet-ing things, to dwell with joy in e-ter--nal a-bodes,__ jus-ti-fy-ing them by faith and__ grace.__\n\nBoth now and ev--er, and un-to the ag--es of ag-es. A-men.\n\nThere is none blame-less as thou art, who art God’s all-pure Moth-er; who a-lone from e-ter-ni-ty con-ceived with-in her womb the great and on-ly true God, Who hath ut-ter-ly de-stroyed the might of__ death.__\n\nThere is none ho-ly as Thou art, Lord my God, Who hast lift-ed up the horn of Thy faith-ful, Thou Whose good-ness hath no end, and hast es-tab-lished them firm on the rock of Thy con-fes-sion for all__ time.___"
    }
  }
